The maintenance agent joins the catalogue, and the SEO, sales, finance, support and project management templates read the sources they name

The owner named six agents a web agency runs, and four of the five templates that already existed for
them read entities nothing registers (`deal`, `project`, `task`, `page`) or tools no source provides
(`ticket.search`, `xero_invoice.search`). Each installed incomplete and disabled on every install, and
completed by hand read nothing from the systems it names: the catalogue said a sales agent existed, and
no install could make one answer. Version 2 of the accountant had already found this in the ledger, and
this is the same fix applied to the rest, with the sixth template written the same way.

What changed, per template, and every version raised because what is on file under a version is never
replaced (brain.ops.builtin_templates), so version 1 of each stays on file as signed:

- maintenance_agent v1 (M13.7.9, new): declares the ticket desk (freshdesk) and the maintenance records
  source (laravel, which needs-rupash 156 A decided is the maintenance portal), the ticket analysis,
  website health check and website troubleshooting skills, the HTTP website check and, as a capability
  because the check opens it from inside itself, the read-only browser. Read-only, and it names no
  department: a department a template names is one company's. Its one workflow and its approval are put on
  the installed agent from the Automations page (needs-rupash 170 A), where a person approves the reply.
- seo_agent v2 (M13.8.7): analytics and search console connectors, the figures each maps, an HTTP check,
  and the SEO audit, keyword research and monthly report skills. Five top queries and five top pages
  rather than ten, because a memory formed while running an agent carries its capabilities as tags and
  tests/unit/test_memory_tables.py holds the column's bound; widening the column is a migration this does
  not need.
- pre_sales v2, support_ticket_agent v2, accountant_agent v3, project_manager v2 (M13.8.8): HubSpot deal
  stage and never its amount, the price list's sell price and never its cost; Freshdesk's real
  `description_text`; Xero's invoice and contact reads and nothing the ledger does not register; and the
  project manager reads tickets and the maintenance records, which is where needs-rupash 137 decided a
  client's work lives.

**Skills are pinned by literal digests, and a test holds them equal to the starter pack.** A SkillRef
pins a digest and the digest is part of what a template's own digest and signature cover. Computed at
import, rewording a starter skill would silently change six templates already on file under the same
version, and an install's own check would find "not as shipped" with nothing in the diff saying why.
Literals make it a deliberate edit: the test goes red on the day the words change.

**One owner question, not decided here.** None of the owner's eight starter skills is about a ledger, so
the finance agent carries no skill, and a ninth would arrive on every install, which
tests/unit/test_starter_skills.py exists to refuse. Rejected: adding one anyway.

The install check (acceptance_checks_role_templates, one check for the three leaves) holds each template
to this install's own registries: on file as shipped, connectors this release ships, skills at the digest
the starter pack furnishes, every tool bound with the website check registered the way the application
registers it, installed from the gallery's route as a disabled agent at Shadow naming its connectors and
skills, and finished again over serving connectors so the real gate starts a run. It assumes nothing
about what an install has connected. Eleven break tests make it fail with its own sentence each.

Reused: brain.agents.template (SkillRef, publish), brain.agents.install (bind_tools, complete, rehearse),
brain.ops.builtin_templates (signing the catalogue), brain.ops.acceptance_checks_templates (the install
route helpers, imported rather than copied), brain.tools.starter_skills (the eight skills), brain.tools.
website_check (the check and its browser), brain.connectors field rules (the classification the
templates are held against). Replaced: the catalogue entries of four templates, by new versions, for the
reason above; tests/unit/test_catalogue.py's ready set, its leaf count and the sales and ledger tests
move with them.

Mutation (brain.ops.mutation, named tests run clean first):
a pinned skill digest no longer the starter pack's          | caught    | test_every_skill_digest_a_template_pins_is_the_one_the_starter_pack_furnishes
a template pins the wrong skill's digest                    | caught    | test_every_skill_digest_a_template_pins_is_the_one_the_starter_pack_furnishes
the maintenance agent loses a skill                         | caught    | test_a_role_template_carries_the_starter_skills_its_role_is_asked_through[maintenance_agent]
the maintenance agent reads a client's contract value       | caught    | test_a_role_template_reads_nothing_classified_above_internal[maintenance_agent]
the maintenance agent loses the read-only browser           | caught    | test_the_maintenance_agent_checks_a_website_over_http_and_may_open_the_read_only_browser[local]
the maintenance agent loses the ticket desk                 | caught    | test_a_role_template_declares_the_connectors_its_leaf_names[maintenance_agent]
the maintenance agent may write                             | caught    | test_a_role_template_reaches_no_further_than_a_read[maintenance_agent]
the sales agent reads a deal's amount                       | caught    | test_a_role_template_reads_nothing_classified_above_internal[pre_sales]
the finance agent reads a contact's tax number              | caught    | test_the_finance_agent_reads_the_amount_owed_and_nothing_else_above_internal
the SEO agent loses the search console                      | caught    | test_a_role_template_declares_the_connectors_its_leaf_names[seo_agent]
the support agent asks for a search no source registers     | caught    | test_a_role_template_installs_ready_and_a_run_through_it_starts[support_ticket_agent-local]
a role template names a read as a write                     | caught    | test_every_capability_a_role_template_names_is_a_field_a_source_maps[maintenance_agent]
the install check stops asking about the SEO agent          | caught    | test_the_catalogues_list_of_role_templates_is_the_six_the_leaves_name
check: a stored template that is not the shipped one passes | caught    | test_a_stored_role_template_that_is_not_the_shipped_one_fails_the_check
check: a template missing from the install passes           | caught    | test_a_role_template_the_release_ships_and_the_install_does_not_hold_fails_the_check
check: a connector nobody ships passes                      | caught    | test_a_role_template_declaring_a_connector_nobody_ships_fails_the_check
check: a skill the starter pack does not furnish passes     | caught    | test_a_role_template_pinning_a_skill_nothing_furnishes_fails_the_check
check: a tool nothing binds passes                          | caught    | test_a_role_template_declaring_a_tool_nothing_binds_fails_the_check
check: an agent installed enabled passes                    | caught    | test_an_install_that_leaves_the_role_agent_enabled_fails_the_check
check: an agent starting above Shadow passes                | caught    | test_an_install_whose_agent_starts_above_shadow_fails_the_check
check: an agent with no connectors named passes             | caught    | test_an_install_that_drops_the_connectors_a_role_template_declares_fails_the_check
check: an agent with no skills pinned passes                | caught    | test_an_install_that_drops_the_skills_a_role_template_pins_fails_the_check
check: an incomplete install with sources serving passes    | caught    | test_a_role_template_that_is_incomplete_with_its_sources_serving_fails_the_check
check: a gate that starts no run passes                     | caught    | test_a_gate_that_starts_no_run_through_a_role_agent_fails_the_check

Verified: the whole of tests/unit/test_acceptance.py ran over a scratch PostgreSQL on a machine with twenty other runs
sharing it; the role template check passed in it, and the only failures were the connector checks that read a source
live under a time limit (analytics, search console, the Laravel views, the maintenance portal), which timed out under
that load and are not touched by this change. CI is where they are judged on an idle runner.

